---
import Layout from '../../layouts/CostmateLegal.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="CostMate — Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of service for the CostMate app by Obura."
>
  <h1>CostMate — Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: August 27, 2026</p>

  <p>
    These terms apply to the CostMate mobile and web application ("the app"),
    published by Obura. By creating an account or using the app you agree to
    these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>What CostMate is</h2>
  <p>
    CostMate is a product-costing tool for small manufacturers: it calculates
    material, equipment and overhead costs from the data you enter. The results
    are estimates based on your own inputs — they are informational and do not
    constitute financial, accounting, or tax advice. Always verify important
    figures before relying on them commercially.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account and your data</h2>
  <p>
    You are responsible for keeping your sign-in credentials safe and for the
    accuracy of the data you enter. Your content belongs to you; we only store
    and process it to provide the service, as described in the
    <a href="/costmate/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. You can delete your
    account and all its data at any time (see
    <a href="/costmate/delete-account/">how</a>).
  </p>

  <h2>Free plan and Pro subscription</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The free plan includes core features with limits (currently one business,
      and caps on the number of materials and products). Limits may change over
      time; existing data is never deleted because of a limit change.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Pro</strong> is an optional auto-renewing subscription that
      removes those limits and adds extra features (for example multiple
      businesses and automatic energy-price updates).
    </li>
    <li>
      Payment is charged to your app store account (Google Play or the App
      Store) at confirmation of purchase. The price is shown in the app before
      you buy.
    </li>
    <li>
      Subscriptions <strong>renew automatically</strong> unless cancelled at
      least 24 hours before the end of the current period. You can cancel any
      time in your app store's subscription settings (Google Play → Payments
      &amp; subscriptions, or App Store → Apple ID → Subscriptions); access
      continues until the end of the paid period.
    </li>
    <li>Refunds are handled by the app store under its own refund policy.</li>
    <li>
      If a subscription ends, your account returns to the free plan. Data
      created while on Pro is kept, but features above the free limits may
      become read-only or unavailable until you subscribe again.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Don't attempt to break, overload, or reverse the service, access other
    users' data, or use the app for unlawful purposes. We may suspend accounts
    that abuse the service.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep the app available and your data safe, but the service is
    provided "as is", without warranties of uninterrupted availability. We may
    add, change, or retire features. If we ever discontinue the service, we
    will give reasonable notice so you can export your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, Obura is not liable for indirect
    damages or for business decisions made based on the app's calculations.
    Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited under
    applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    If these terms change materially, the updated version will be published at
    this address with a new "last updated" date; continued use of the app after
    that constitutes acceptance.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href="mailto:info@obura.io">info@obura.io</a></p>

  <p class="muted">
    See also: <a href="/costmate/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> ·
    <a href="/costmate/delete-account/">Delete your account</a>
  </p>
</Layout>
